  "note": "Meta-Llama-3-8B ships a tiktoken-style byte-level BPE with a 128000-entry vocabulary and 256 added_tokens (all special:true) at ids 128000-128255 (<|begin_of_text|>, <|end_of_text|>, <|start_header_id|>, <|end_header_id|>, <|eot_id|>, and 251 <|reserved_special_token_N|> slots). Major shape change from Llama-2: no SentencePiece byte_fallback, no normalizer, no Prepend - the pipeline is Split(Regex, cl100k_base-family split pattern) + ByteLevel pre_tokenizer + Sequence[ByteLevel, TemplateProcessing(<|begin_of_text|>)] post_processor. The 20 cases span ASCII prose / code / CJK / Cyrillic / emoji / whitespace / long inputs plus Llama-3's chat-format surface forms (raw <|begin_of_text|>hi<|end_of_text|> and the <|start_header_id|>/<|eot_id|> header markers). Reference ids come from transformers.PreTrainedTokenizerFast against the local NousResearch mirror tokenizer.json (byte-identical to the gated upstream) - pass criterion is byte-for-byte parity.",
